# The whole metadata record in ONE call, without blocking. The clean uniform interface, the per-env native
# implementation selected at build time and hidden.
#
# Beside [../metadata.tree](../metadata.tree), which is the synchronous surface and answers one field at a time.
# A separate module rather than a task in that one, because a dock is paid for by whoever imports the module: a
# program asking `is-directory` should not link swift-nio for it.

load @term/seed/code/native/{platform}/file/asynchronous/metadata
  find meta-read

load @term/seed/code/file/metadata
  find file-metadata

# With `follow`, a symbolic link is followed and the record describes what it points at; without it, the link
# itself. One stat, rather than the three the synchronous module would take.
task read
  note async
  take path, like text
  take
    follow
    like boolean
    fall true
  like file-metadata
  send back
    call meta-read
      read path
      read follow
      wait true
